# One-off Moss probes. They exist to PROVE that Moss's `score` is a degenerate
# reciprocal-rank artefact, so they are the only files in the tree that read
# `.score`. They are not part of the build (outside tsconfig include) and must not
# be committed: the cardinal rule is that a `.score` read outside a comment is a
# defect, and a reviewer greps for exactly that.
research/moss-probes/
